# Local development against the REAL Cognito pool.
#
# Setting all three flips web/src/auth/provider.ts from the local issuer to
# the hosted UI, with RS256 verification against the pool's published JWKS.
# Remove them (or this file) to get the four demo accounts back.
#
# Gitignored. `terraform output vercel_env` in infra/terraform/auth prints them.
# Vite reads .env at STARTUP - restart the dev server after editing.

VITE_COGNITO_DOMAIN=meridian-demo-auth.auth.us-east-1.amazoncognito.com
VITE_COGNITO_CLIENT_ID=39k7f00f8ok9k09muoe6sjobvh
VITE_COGNITO_ISSUER=https://cognito-idp.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/us-east-1_0d9Xr0qXI

# Which IdPs the pool actually has. Home-realm discovery maps
# acme-freight.com to AcmeSAML, which this pool does NOT have - without this
# list the board asks for it and Cognito answers "Login option is not
# available". Add Google here once its credentials are in terraform.tfvars.
VITE_COGNITO_IDPS=COGNITO

# RENAMED to .env.local.cognito so the board uses the offline issuer and the
# four demo accounts - which is what a client demo needs, since nobody has a
# Cognito password. Rename back to `.env.local` and restart Vite to return to
# the real pool. The pool, trigger and membership table are all still deployed.
